  "context_markdown": "This register records known, intentional differences between the supplied printed source and this working edition. Entries follow movement and local bar order. The choices are adopted for this edition; they do not claim to reconstruct the original transcriber's intentions.\n\nAll four movements and all 18 pages of the supplied scan were compared with the 19-page native MuseScore engraving, with magnified checks of identified passages. This is a source comparison, not a new critical edition or a guarantee that every small mark has been independently verified. The source is the Breitkopf & Härtel collected edition, reprinted by Dover, not an autograph.\n\nBar numbers restart with each movement. Upbeats are unnumbered (shown as 0 in the data); first and second endings and split pickup bars can share printed numbers. The source itself has no printed bar numbers. Images show representative passages, with separate source and edition pagination.",
